xnu 0273: count the interval between frames, not just the rate

A rate hides cadence: 60 swaps a second is smooth if they land 16.6 ms apart and
a stutter if they alternate 12/22, and the panel picks a frame up at the next
vsync, so what the eye sees is the gap, not the average. Each swap now records
the interval since the previous one and the fps line prints `gap avg`/`gap max`
with the number of intervals in 20-33 ms (a frame that slipped) and over 33 ms
(a frame lost). `fLastSwapTicks` is zeroed with the other counters only after the
line is printed, so the first gap of each second is the real one.

